          "block_id": "tile_sql_fund_relational_select.r02.b01",
          "role": "misconception",
          "text": "The FROM clause names the table to read — it does not choose columns. The SELECT list names the columns (or expressions) that appear in the output — it does not name the table. SELECT name, city FROM customers: the SELECT list picks two columns; FROM customers supplies all the rows.",
